WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.100
The Skeld-class star ship Innobis was still,
suspended against a backdrop of stars and

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.840
the colorful glow of distant nebulas.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:14.300
Frozen in the inky void of deep space, calm;
at least from the outside.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:19.510
But inside the main hull of the ship, was
far from the silent stillness of the stars.

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:24.710
Pandemonium hit as the sounds of a claxon
reverberated through metal corridors, each

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:28.530
wail punctuated by the flash of blood-red
warning lights.

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:34.180
Blue looked up at the blinking, strobing color,
and instantly knew what it meant.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:38.750
“Emergency meeting,” he muttered to himself,
behind the visor of his spacesuit.

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:43.760
Blue turned heel and ran, his boots clanging
against the metal floor of the corridor.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:48.879
He ran as fast as he could in his spacesuit,
arriving panting to the cafeteria.

00:00:48.879 --> 00:00:53.969
His breathless wheezes fogged up his visor,
but beyond, he could still see the other six

00:00:53.969 --> 00:00:55.610
fellow members of the ship’s crew.

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:58.410
Or at least, he thought all six of them were
there.

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:02.449
It was only as he walked closer that he spotted
someone was missing.

00:01:02.449 --> 00:01:07.500
White, Red, Green, Orange, Yellow, and now
Blue were all present…

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.850
but where was Pink?

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:11.080
“You took your time, Blue,” White declared.

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:14.420
“I was over at the Lower Engine,” he panted
back.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:17.479
“It’s further away, sorry I’m late – ran
as fast as I could.”

00:01:17.479 --> 00:01:19.250
“What’s the situation here?”

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:20.250
Orange asked.

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:23.770
“Well, I think we should wait for Pink to
get here before we get into-” Red started

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:25.610
to say, only to be interrupted.

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:28.950
“That’s why I called the meeting,” Green
announced.

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:30.870
“Pink has gone missing.”

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:32.590
“B-but that’s impossible!”

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:35.079
Red immediately responded, drawing a glare
from White.

00:01:35.079 --> 00:01:38.700
“I saw Pink only a few moments ago, we were
both tell over in Electrical.”

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:42.550
To Blue, along with some of the others, that
seemed a little bit odd.

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:47.850
If Red and pink had been close to each other,
then how had Green known to call the Emergency

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:48.850
Meeting?

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:54.230
The room erupted into a brief debate, with
White implying in a rather spiteful way that

00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:56.640
Red knew more than he was letting on.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:00.660
Interjecting, Blue suggested they all split
up and search for Pink, which was quickly

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:01.950
shot down.

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:06.570
White reminded the rest of the crewmates that
their ship was in need of constant maintenance.

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:11.210
If they didn’t perform the necessary tasks
to keep it running, then the Innobis would

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:13.090
never reach its destination.

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:16.060
“Report back here when you’re finished,”
White barked.

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:20.460
As they all split off, Blue couldn’t help
wondering what had gotten White more agitated

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:21.460
than normal.

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:25.920
However, little did any of the crew aboard
the Innobis realize, but they had picked up

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.310
a stowaway.

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:30.989
The creature had been slipping through the
ventilation system, curiously watching the

00:02:30.989 --> 00:02:35.720
assembled group in the cafeteria before they
broke away and headed off to various different

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:37.420
areas of the ship.

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:41.879
Spotting one of the crewmates, a man wearing
a bright orange spacesuit, the thing in the

00:02:41.879 --> 00:02:46.970
vents felt oddly drawn to him, and slithered
off down the vents in the direction Orange

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:47.970
had been heading.

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:53.130
Now, while you might be forgiven for at first
expecting this extra passenger to be some

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:58.220
kind of alien parasite that uses human bodies
as hosts before bursting out of their chest

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:03.170
only to them proceed to kill everything in
sight, then you’d be sorely mistaken.

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:06.430
Stand down, Sigourney, there are no Xenomorphs
aboard this ship.

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:11.470
No, this slippery little stowaway was none
other than the lovable blob of orange slime

00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:17.549
known as SCP-999, otherwise referred to as
the Tickle Monster.

00:03:17.549 --> 00:03:22.970
Known for being an adorable, amorphous anomaly,
resembling a pile of gelatinous orange matter,

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:29.270
SCP-999 has long been considered one of the
most harmless and affection SCPs ever cataloged.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:33.760
It has a habit of honing in on the nearest
person, and leaping right at them.

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:38.640
Not as a means to attack them, or attach any
scary eight-legged egg-laying head-hugging

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:41.310
creature to any faces.

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:46.989
Instead, SCP-999 offers a loving embrace and
wholesome nuzzling to a person's face, all

00:03:46.989 --> 00:03:52.400
while emitting soothing gurgling and cooing
noises, as well as pleasant scents that change

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:57.170
depending on what the person it’s hugging
finds most appealing or calming.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:04:02.569
While not in any way harmful, and only ever
acting out of the most well-meant intentions,

00:04:02.569 --> 00:04:07.250
SCP-999 had been the one responsible for Pink’s
disappearance.

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:11.000
The Tickle Monster had been discovered by
Pink while he was traveling through a corridor

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:14.549
past the MedBay, taking the longer route back
to Electrical.

00:04:14.549 --> 00:04:19.220
There, SCP-999 had playfully pounced on the
crewmate to offer a hug.

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:24.819
This had caused Pink to experience the full
effect of SCP-999’s anomalous properties,

00:04:24.819 --> 00:04:27.660
slipping into an overwhelmingly elated state.

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:33.300
So, while not currently injured, he was calmly
relaxing in a hidden corner of the MedBay…

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:37.490
with the rest of the crew completely unaware
of what was going on.

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:43.070
SCP-999 had spotted orange, and had been able
to recognize the same color as its own jello-like

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:44.070
body.

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:48.360
Drawn to the crewmate, the Tickle Monster
snuck towards Orange while his back was turned,

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:51.460
busy cleaning out the filters in the O2 chamber.

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:56.710
Before he could turn around and spot the creature,
Orange was leaped at by SCP-999, and lured

00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:58.650
into the Medbay with Pink…

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:04.099
Not long after, Blue had finished up his latest
task, fixing up the wiring in Storage.

00:05:04.099 --> 00:05:08.900
Brushing off his hands, he began casually
walking back in the direction of the cafeteria,

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:12.030
only to see the crimson of Red’s spacesuit
zip past.

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:18.479
He was rushing down the corridor, almost like
he had just been caught – well, red-handed.

00:05:18.479 --> 00:05:21.580
Something didn’t seem right, Blue thought
to himself.

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:25.300
Red had seemed pretty indignant earlier when
Pink had vanished.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:29.539
Although he couldn’t say with any certainty
if it was because Red really did know what

00:05:29.539 --> 00:05:32.740
was going on, or if they were just nervous.

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:37.139
Returning to the cafeteria, however, the crew
quickly realized that Orange was now gone

00:05:37.139 --> 00:05:38.139
too.

00:05:38.139 --> 00:05:40.060
“I’m calling it now,” White declared.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:41.130
“This was you, Red.

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:42.210
You’re up to something!”

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:43.970
“I swear, I’m not!”

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:48.270
Red pleaded – it was hard to see how sincere
his expression was through the tinted space

00:05:48.270 --> 00:05:49.270
helmet visor.

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:53.169
“Well, if anyone else knows anything, or
saw anything, then come forward,” White

00:05:53.169 --> 00:05:54.550
said to the group.

00:05:54.550 --> 00:05:59.259
The rest of the crew were awkwardly shuffling
on their feet, each one clearly uncertain

00:05:59.259 --> 00:06:03.170
but nobody wanting to come forward and be
the first to speak.

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:04.640
“Actually, I…”

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:06.150
Blue found themselves saying.

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:10.199
“I saw Red dashing around in the corridor,
he seemed like he was in the hurry.

00:06:10.199 --> 00:06:12.419
Or maybe like he was… up to something?

00:06:12.419 --> 00:06:14.630
Maybe, look it doesn’t prove anything.”

00:06:14.630 --> 00:06:16.870
“You don’t know that,” Yellow chimed
in.

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:19.680
“Who knows, he might have been eyeing you
up as he next victim!”

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:20.680
“Victim?”

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:21.680
Red exclaimed.

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:24.580
“Look, I don’t like what you’re implying
here, I haven’t killed anyone.”

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:27.789
“Nobody said Pink and Orange were dead,”
White replied.

00:06:27.789 --> 00:06:30.039
“Unless you know more than you’re letting
on.”

00:06:30.039 --> 00:06:34.800
“I swear, I don’t know what’s happening,
I’m just as in the dark as you all are!”

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:35.800
Red insisted.

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:39.229
“In that case, prove it,” Green interjected
bluntly.

00:06:39.229 --> 00:06:42.110
“Prove you didn’t kill Orange and Pink.”

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:43.110
“How?”

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:44.110
Red yelled.

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:45.110
“How can I prove that?”

00:06:45.110 --> 00:06:49.599
“You could prove they’re both still alive,”
said Yellow – completely unaware that Pink

00:06:49.599 --> 00:06:52.210
and Orange were actually still alive.

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:55.090
“He can’t prove it,” White announced
solemnly.

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:58.120
“Because I bet they’re not even on the
ship anymore…”

00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:01.889
The missing crewmates were, in actuality,
still aboard the ship; in fact, they were

00:07:01.889 --> 00:07:05.389
having the time of their lives inside the
MedBay with SCP-999.

00:07:05.389 --> 00:07:09.340
But that hadn’t stopped the rest of the
crew turning on Red.

00:07:09.340 --> 00:07:11.550
“Come on, Red,” Blue sighed.

00:07:11.550 --> 00:07:14.259
“I mean, you’ve got to admit you’re
acting a little…

00:07:14.259 --> 00:07:16.610
well, not suspicious, but definitely evasive.”

00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:20.380
"Oh, sure, what just because I’m wearing
red you all think I’m some kind of murderous

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:21.380
traitor?”

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:24.979
Red shouted, his desperate, pleading tears
obscured by his helmet’s visor.

00:07:24.979 --> 00:07:25.979
“This is McCarthyism!”

00:07:25.979 --> 00:07:29.099
“Look, why don’t you just give a straight
answer?”

00:07:29.099 --> 00:07:33.380
Blue offered, trying to remain reasonable
and not to join the rapidly growing witch

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:34.380
hunt.

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:35.389
“Because I’m scared!”

00:07:35.389 --> 00:07:36.389
Red insisted.

00:07:36.389 --> 00:07:38.040
“Scared that we’ll find out?”

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:40.410
White yelled, leaping at Red and pinning him
down.

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:42.630
“Quick, the rest of you grab his arms and
legs!”

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:47.659
A struggle ensued, with Red desperately kicking
and flailing about, while Green and Yellow

00:07:47.659 --> 00:07:49.230
gripped an arm and leg.

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:54.900
Blue was reluctant, he wanted to urge everyone
to calm down and not do anything irrational.

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:59.110
But it was already too late; if he opposed,
the blame might shift to him.

00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:03.629
Under White’s direction, the crew lifted
Red up and carried him to the Innobis’ outer

00:08:03.629 --> 00:08:04.629
airlock.

00:08:04.629 --> 00:08:08.650
They threw Red past the inside door, which
slammed shut behind him as he turned and started

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:12.479
slamming his hand against the surface, begging
for them to let him out.

00:08:12.479 --> 00:08:16.090
His pleas fell on deaf ears as White threw
a nearby switch.

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:20.979
The outer door of the airlock opened, the
vacuum of space pulling Red out of the ship,

00:08:20.979 --> 00:08:26.340
practically firing him out of the hull like
a cannon, leaving him to drift away, alone

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:29.520
and with limited oxygen in his spacesuit.

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:33.200
“Right, now that imposter’s been dealt
with, everyone get back to work,” White

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:34.200
announced.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:36.510
“We need to keep this ship in a fit state
to move.”

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:40.370
Blue was speechless; he’d thought they were
just going to hold Red prisoner in a secure

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:42.460
part of the ship until he calmed down.

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:46.270
Instead, he’d aided his crewmates in murdering
one of their own.

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:50.490
Even the very thought of it made Blue feel
sick – and he would have been if he wasn’t

00:08:50.490 --> 00:08:51.490
wearing a space helmet.

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:56.680
It had all happened so fast, he’d barely
had enough time to consider all the facts.

00:08:56.680 --> 00:09:01.870
After all, White had seemed adamant, from
the very start, that Red was somehow responsible

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:04.220
for Orange and Pink disappearing.

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:07.900
But he had no concrete evidence to base that
assumption on.

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:10.310
Then again, where were those missing crewmates?

00:09:10.310 --> 00:09:14.920
There had been no sign of them, no bodies
or discarded suits.

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:17.339
Maybe they weren’t on the ship at all anymore.

00:09:17.339 --> 00:09:20.090
What if White was right and Red had killed
them?

00:09:20.090 --> 00:09:21.300
Or worse…

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:25.360
what if White had been the one responsible,
and Blue had just helped him kill an innocent

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:28.140
spaceman to cover up his cruel misdeeds.

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:32.910
Of course, the surviving crew were so wrapped
up in the horrifying moral and ethical implications

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:36.850
of the situation that none of them thought
to check the Medbay.

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:41.910
Meanwhile, SCP-999 had found two more new
friends, Green and Yellow.

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:46.120
The pair had seemed rather glum – since
they just helped to kill Red – and so the

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:48.880
orange blob of good vibes had sought them
out.

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:53.360
Now, the two of them – plus Orange and Pink,
who were still fine – were all enjoying

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:55.940
the company of the Tickle Monster in the MedBay.

00:09:55.940 --> 00:10:01.899
At the same time, though, Blue was returning
from his task of uploading data over in Admin…

00:10:01.899 --> 00:10:05.420
To find only White left, waiting for him in
the cafeteria.

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:09.209
Neither one said anything, they’d both already
made up their minds.

00:10:09.209 --> 00:10:14.850
In each one’s head, the other was the real
guilty party, the culprit responsible for

00:10:14.850 --> 00:10:19.339
the disappearances – and apparent deaths
– of their other crewmates.

00:10:19.339 --> 00:10:24.940
Both Blue and White were convinced that the
other was truly the imposter among us.

00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:31.540
Enraged, they charged at each other; rather
than act rationally, maybe by sticking together

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:36.690
and searching the rest of the ship, the two
spacemen engaged each other in a scuffle.

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:37.690
“You’re sus!”

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:41.329
Blue roared, punching White in the stomach,
causing him to stagger backwards.

00:10:41.329 --> 00:10:46.100
“I’m not the one who’s sus,” White
wheezed, rushing back towards Blue and shoulder

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:48.250
barging him to the cafeteria floor.

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:50.350
“You are, you’re sus, Blue!”

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:54.589
They continued their scrap, trading blows
until Blue was able to throw a punch that

00:10:54.589 --> 00:10:56.760
cracked the glass visor of White’s helmet.

00:10:56.760 --> 00:11:01.290
There was a hiss as the air escaped, and while
White desperately fumbled with his helmet,

00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:06.029
trying to plug the crack, Blue was able to
grab him by his oxygen tank and drag him towards

00:11:06.029 --> 00:11:07.079
the airlock.

00:11:07.079 --> 00:11:12.570
Blasting his adversary out into the unforgiving
cold, emptiness of space, Blue staggered through

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:13.570
the ship.

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:17.420
He was certain that he’d received a broken
rib during the fight, and hobbled along the

00:11:17.420 --> 00:11:19.220
corridors towards the Medbay.

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:22.910
When the entrance open, he stared in disbelief
at what he saw.

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:27.620
Sat inside were the entire crew – minus
the pair who’d been ejected from the airlock,

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:28.620
of course.

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:33.649
Pink, Orange, Green, and Yellow were playing
with a friendly blob of orange slime, that

00:11:33.649 --> 00:11:37.010
seemed to have the energy and enthusiasm of
a pet dog.

00:11:37.010 --> 00:11:41.740
The crewmates were laughing, hugging the Tickle
Monster, and engaging it in tickle fights,

00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:44.120
clearly in a state of heightened elation.

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:48.840
In a sudden instant of realization, the horror
caught up with Blue; he had just murdered

00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:51.130
White, and Red… for nothing.

00:11:51.130 --> 00:11:52.209
Both of them were innocent.

00:11:52.209 --> 00:11:55.350
In fact, nobody on the ship was actually missing.

00:11:55.350 --> 00:12:01.350
Just before this horrifying epiphany caused
Blue to suffer an emotional breakdown, SCP-999

00:12:01.350 --> 00:12:04.209
glided across the floor towards him, smiling.

00:12:04.209 --> 00:12:08.220
As he knelt to pat the orange blob on the
head, Blue suddenly felt better about the

00:12:08.220 --> 00:12:10.870
two deaths he’d been responsible for.

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:16.050
Actually, he felt great, compelled to start
giggling uncontrollably as he joined his fellow

00:12:16.050 --> 00:12:19.959
surviving crewmates in playing with the stowaway
SCP-999.

00:12:19.959 --> 00:12:25.970
Although, thanks to that delightful distraction,
not one of the remaining astronauts realized

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:30.910
that their ship was still adrift in space…
heading right towards a sun.

00:12:30.910 --> 00:12:37.470
Now go and check out “SCP-999 THE TICKLE
MONSTER” and “SCP-5167- WHEN THE IMPOSTER

00:12:37.470 --> 00:12:40.350
IS SUS” for more blobs and imposters!

